Hi,

Thanks for your help. The if i < K condition cannot work as well since K is not a constant.
What I am going to do is taking K as a variable which follows a Poisson distribution.
Something like this:

K ~ Poisson(lambda),
pi[1:K] ~ Dirichlet(gamma, ...)
for (i in 1:N){
y[i] ~ Normal(mu[z[i]], tau[z[i]])
z[i] ~ categorical(pi[1:K])
}
for (j in 1:K) {mu[j] ~ Normal(...); tau[j] ~ Invgamma(...)}

Thanks,
Zhihua

